&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 1&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50074766</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:49:57 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Mac Markdown reader for your AI agents</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50074607</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi HN, I'm Kirill.&lt;p&gt;A dozen coding agents running in parallel, producing walls of suggestions, comments and ideas, all at once, all crammed into 88 columns of terminal scrollback, all gone the moment you run the next command. Does this sound familiar?&lt;p&gt;FolderMd (&lt;a href="https://foldermd.com" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://foldermd.com&lt;/a&gt;) might be for you. It's free, and it's fast, and your agents can use it. I made it because I just couldn't handle it anymore.&lt;p&gt;It's a small Mac app that gives those documents a home. Agents read our explainer and then learn to write markdown into a .foldermd/, instead of writing it into the terminal. FolderMD then opens each one instantly and renders it like a book: real typography, syntax-highlighted code, Mermaid diagrams, light and dark mode.&lt;p&gt;You can edit a doc and save it, you can then add comments just like you would in Google Doc, and pass those comments to the agent.&lt;p&gt;Let me know what you think, and if you want to see any features, and improvements. Thanks! -K.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
